From 33f3f55d43237d0ce5958f558741bb776020b356 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:12:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 47/52] Parse schematics of KiCad's 10.99 development version
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

KiCad's master branch has added a number of things to the schematic and
symbol library formats since 10.0, which gerbonara could not load:

- custom properties, (custom_property "name" "value"), on almost
  every item, and (locked yes) on most schematic items
- hatched fills: hatch, reverse_hatch and cross_hatch
- line end decorations such as arrows, (start_shape ...) and
  (end_shape ...), on lines, polylines, arcs and Bézier curves
- ellipses and elliptical arcs, in schematics and symbols, which are also
  exported to SVG
- embedded files in schematics and library symbols
- net chains
- footprint associations and pin maps of library symbols, and pin map
  overrides of placed symbols and their variants
- the passthrough setting and variant symbol overrides of placed symbols
- directive_label, which KiCad reads as a netclass flag
- schematic groups, which write (locked yes) after the name, unlike
  PCB groups

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
